# Test that macro transformers can safely return AST dicts through the
# deep_materialize output boundary without errors.
#
# What this exercises: the output deep_materialize at the macro expansion
# boundary runs on the dict returned by the transformer and correctly
# traverses all ThunkIds in the output Value::Dict. The transformer returns
# a shallow AST dict with primitive field values (Value::Bool), which
# validates the happy path of the boundary with no lazy thunks.
#
# Note: `true` here is a parser literal (Value::Bool), not a prelude binding.
# Environment stores Rc<Thunk> (not ThunkId), so closure captures from the
# prelude env do not leak ThunkIds between arenas. The cross-arena panic
# requires a ThunkId from the stdlib arena to end up inside a Value::Dict
# or Value::Seq in the transformer output — which this test does not
# produce (primitives contain no ThunkId).

[defmacro const-true [args]
  # Returns an AST dict for the literal `true`.
  # The dict itself (Value::Dict with ThunkIds) is traversed by
  # deep_materialize at the output boundary.
  [type: "literal"  kind: "bool"  value: true]
]

[const-true 42]
=== out
Bool(true)
